Z||000000||Cozmo||08-03-2001||06:19 AM||||I have a few sets of pre-'88 factory diamond rims laying around, been toying with some ideas...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-035F.JPG"> <BR>(excuse the thumb over part of the lens, that's not part of the mods <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>I painted the center area gloss black.  Polished the rim edges and the top surfaces of the diamond pattern (still not fully polished yet, they'll look better when shined to a mirror finish).<BR>Added some Cragar spinners (they fit perfectly with the supplied mounting hardware).<BR>I'm thinking about adding some chrome rivets in the little notches on the outer edge of the diamond pattern kind of like a modular type wheel.  Maybe drill and tap for some nice domed allen head screws.<BR>From what I can tell, this shouldn't interfere with the wheel holding air, but I don't want to ruin a good wheel.<BR>Would this work, and if so what do you people think?<BR>Bob C.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-03-2001||06:36 AM||||First of all, you've got to take that fake spinner thing off that wheel.  Whew!  Now that that's done, I don't see why drilling and tapping a few small holes would make any difference.  I wouldn't go any deeper than I had to though.  I thought about polishing the tops of the lace, too but I was told that the wheel would never finish right.  Something about being too rough.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
